MASTER BUILD PROMPT — COMPLETE ANDROID LAUNCHER

PROJECT: TOTAL LAUNCHER REIMAGINED

Build a complete, production-quality Android home screen replacement that reproduces the functionality, customization depth, flexibility, and feature set of Total Launcher, while adding a significantly more advanced application organization, categorization, tagging, drawer, and navigation system.

This is a full application development assignment, NOT a prototype, demonstration, landing page, web app, or simplified launcher.

The objective is to create an independent Android launcher that can replace the device's default home screen and provide everything Total Launcher provides, plus the additional capabilities specified below.

Do not implement a simplified interpretation. Do not omit features. Do not defer features to future development. Do not create a staged development plan. Implement the complete application and all requested systems in this build.

1. PLATFORM AND TECHNICAL FOUNDATION

Target platform:

- Android phones and tablets.
- Primary test device: Google Pixel 9.
- Android 17 compatibility.
- Responsive portrait and landscape layouts.
- Foldable-device compatibility where supported.

Preferred technology:

- Kotlin.
- Jetpack Compose.
- Native Android APIs.
- Room database.
- DataStore.
- Android AppWidget framework.
- Android PackageManager.
- Android Storage Access Framework.

The application must:

- Function as a real Android launcher.
- Register as an available default Home application.
- Display and launch installed applications.
- Support Android system navigation and lifecycle.
- Support third-party Android widgets.
- Operate without root.
- Work offline.
- Require no account.
- Require no subscription.
- Avoid unnecessary background processes.
- Persist all user configurations.

Do not build a browser-based imitation.

Do not use a website inside a WebView as the primary launcher interface.

Do not use simulated applications, fake widgets, placeholder functionality, or hardcoded app lists.

Use actual Android installed-application data.

