6. NIAGARA-STYLE WAVE ALPHABET NAVIGATION

Implement a vertical alphabetical navigation bar inspired by Niagara Launcher's distinctive interactive alphabet navigation.

This is a required feature.

Place the alphabet index along the RIGHT EDGE of the application drawer by default.

Allow users to move it to the left edge.

The interaction must reproduce the characteristic wave-style navigation behavior, not merely display a static list of letters.

A. Wave behavior

Display alphabet letters vertically.

When the user touches or drags along the alphabet:

- The selected letter enlarges.
- Nearby letters scale progressively.
- Letters above and below create a smooth wave effect.
- The wave follows the user's finger.
- The selected letter is visually highlighted.
- The application list scrolls continuously to the corresponding alphabetical section.

The effect should be smooth, fluid, responsive, and visually polished.

Use animated scaling and spacing adjustments.

Avoid jitter, lag, or delayed scrolling.

B. Alphabet functionality

- Support A–Z.
- Support a # section for numbers and symbols.
- Skip letters with no matching applications or show them as inactive.
- Display a floating letter indicator while navigating.
- Support direct tapping.
- Support continuous dragging.
- Support fast scrolling.
- Support alphabetical grouping.
- Work with both grid and list layouts.
- Respect the currently selected category or tag.
- Recalculate available letters for filtered results.

The wave index must navigate the currently displayed collection, not the entire unfiltered application list.

C. Customization

Allow:

- Left/right placement.
- Alphabet size.
- Selected letter size.
- Wave intensity.
- Animation speed.
- Spacing.
- Color.
- Transparency.
